# Template for this stack's shared/secrets.env on prodbox. Copy to
# /opt/apps/pitchbox-landing/prod/shared/secrets.env, fill in the real ORIGIN,
# `chmod 600` it. release.sh reads this file and copies it (plus the release-pinned
# LANDING_IMAGE/APP_VERSION/APP_COMMIT) into every releases/<sha>/.env, but never
# writes to this file itself. This file is never committed; only this template is.
#
# There is genuinely nothing secret in this stack today: no database and no mail
# sender, because the way in is an account on app.pitchbox.app (decided on #423), so
# ORIGIN is the only variable this file carries. It stays a file rather than a
# hardcoded default so whatever lands after this issue and needs its own config (a
# real second stack on the reserved 5284, an analytics key, anything else scoped to
# this repo) has one place to add it without touching release.sh.
#
# Port convention: 5184 is this repo's prod stack, verified free on prodbox on
# 2026-09-09; pitchbox itself owns 5180-5183 (that repo's scripts/deploy.sh) and
# canonry-landing owns 5195/5295. 5284 is reserved for a second stack under this
# repo, not yet built - see docker/Caddyfile.example.

LANDING_PORT=5184

ORIGIN=https://landing.pitchbox.app
